From ed4c69c30f231723078f9d754c0a3253770d74e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 360/488] soh: name the 21 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_jya_cobra.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 21 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Jya_Cobra/z_bg_jya_cobra.c.

  * func_808958F0 -> BgJyaCobra_RotateVecY
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rotates src about the Y axis by a
    caller-supplied sine and cosine, leaving y alone

  * func_80895A70 -> BgJyaCobra_UpdateLightBeam
    deduced, confidence HIGH: points this statue's MirRay at its beam origin
    and marks it unlit when the brightness falls to zero

  * func_80895BEC -> BgJyaCobra_CarryPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rotates the recorded player offset with the
    statue so the player rides it while it turns

  * func_80895C74 -> BgJyaCobra_UpdateBeamParams
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sets the beam brightness from the puzzle flags
    and the statue's alignment, and recomputes the beam origin and length

  * func_80896918 -> BgJyaCobra_SetupIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: snaps the statue onto its 0x2000 detent and
    installs the idle action

  * func_80896950 -> BgJyaCobra_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the frames the player pushes against
    the statue and starts a turn at 15

  * func_808969F8 -> BgJyaCobra_SetupTurn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: chooses the turn direction from the push angle
    and records the player's offset for the ride

  * func_80896ABC -> BgJyaCobra_Turn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sweeps 0x2000 with an accelerating step,
    carrying the player, then returns to idle on the next detent

  * func_80896CB4 -> BgJyaCobra_DrawMirrorSurface
    deduced, confidence GUESS: draws gCobra2DL in the XLU pass with no color
    or matrix of its own; the display list name gives no hint beyond that it
    is the second cobra piece

  * func_80896D78 -> BgJyaCobra_DrawLightBeam
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gCobra3DL at the beam origin, stretched
    by the beam length and faded by the beam brightness

  * D_80897308 -> sBeamPitchOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-params X rotation added to the beam
    direction and to the beam model, all zero in the shipped table

  * D_80897310 -> sBeamDimsWithAngle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-params flag enabling the misalignment
    dimming in BgJyaCobra_UpdateBeamParams

  * D_80897314 -> sBeamAlignedYaws
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-params yaw the statue is measured against
    when dimming the beam

  * D_8089731C -> sShadowBrushLarge
    deduced, confidence HIGH: 11x11 alpha brush stamped along the statue
    outline when building the shadow texture

  * D_80897398 -> sShadowBrushSmall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: 3x3 alpha brush stamped along the base outline
    of the same shadow texture

  * D_808973A4 -> sShadowStatueOutline
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 26 points of the cobra silhouette traced
    with sShadowBrushLarge

  * D_808974DC -> sShadowBaseOutline
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 5 points of the pedestal outline traced
    with sShadowBrushSmall

  * D_80897518 -> sShadowBaseRowAlphas
    deduced, confidence HIGH: minimum alpha for each of the four shadow rows
    that form the pedestal bar

  * D_80897538 -> sShadowRotParams0
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the shadow's rotation for the params 0 statue,
    drawn 50 units west of it

  * D_80897540 -> sShadowRotParams2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the shadow's rotation for the params 2 statue,
    drawn 70 units east of it

  * D_80897548 -> sShadowScales
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-params scale applied to the shadow quad

